# Everyone appends to the same place in the changelog, so a plain three-way merge
# conflicts constantly (CHANGELOG.md is touched by ~43% of commits). The union driver
# keeps both sides of a conflicting hunk instead of raising a conflict, which is the
# right answer for an unordered bullet list. The seeded headings in [Unreleased] do the
# rest: entries under different headings already merge cleanly without any driver.
#
# Union never conflicts, so it cannot ask a human. The one case it gets wrong -- a
# branch open across a release re-adding entries that shipped meanwhile -- is caught by
# the "changelog" CI job (scripts/changelog.py check-duplicates).
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
